; ches_screen is the Bonsai-free screen model: the cell mapping, layout geometry,
; scrolling, animation, the UI state and its transition, and the rendered frame as styled text
; spans. It must not depend on bonsai or bonsai_term, so headless tests can drive it.
; It uses notty only for [Notty.Tty_width_hint], the width table notty itself draws
; with, so that our cell counts agree with what reaches the terminal.
; It may use the pure VCS libraries (ches_vcs, ches_vcs_git: core only, no Async, no
; Unix) for the VCS view; never ches_vcs_host, which runs processes (ches_ui owns it).

(library
 (name ches_screen)
 (libraries ches_error ches_app ches_core ches_input ches_highlight ches_palette ches_file_picker ches_file_preview_model ches_line_picker ches_content_picker ches_tile ches_vcs ches_vcs_git core notty-community)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_jane)))
